WEBVTT

00:04.340 --> 00:06.110
I won't accept it!

00:06.110 --> 00:10.350
He can't die without my say-so!

00:12.120 --> 00:13.740
You're alive...

00:13.740 --> 00:17.150
The black turtle is alive!

00:17.580 --> 00:20.410
I'll never let you go again!

00:23.250 --> 00:26.040
Black Turtle, we're getting out of here.

00:26.040 --> 00:28.670
We're gonna climb the Tower 
with the blue turtle.

00:29.730 --> 00:31.420
Rak, I—

00:31.420 --> 00:32.980
What was that sound?

00:33.770 --> 00:34.540
Intruders?

00:34.540 --> 00:36.490
This way! Hurry!

00:36.490 --> 00:38.930
I can't leave yet, so—

00:38.930 --> 00:42.470
No way! I'm taking you home, no matter what!

00:43.430 --> 00:44.570
Come on. Let's go.

00:44.570 --> 00:47.940
Let me go! Hey! I said let me go!

00:46.310 --> 00:47.940
Thank you.

00:47.940 --> 00:51.610
In exchange, we're going 
on a date once you're back!

00:48.430 --> 00:51.560
Ghost Eyeball Turtle! Hey! Let me go!

00:52.090 --> 00:53.190
A date?

00:55.700 --> 01:00.200
Let me go! Ghost Eyeball Turtle! Hat Turtle!

00:56.060 --> 00:58.200
Damn it, keep still!

01:00.610 --> 01:01.700
Black Turtle!

01:21.890 --> 01:23.720
Horyang...

01:23.970 --> 01:25.570
Lord Devil!

01:23.970 --> 01:25.570
Mister!

01:29.420 --> 01:31.910
Hey, let's go find some meat to eat!

01:31.910 --> 01:32.620
Huh?

01:36.700 --> 01:40.270
Uh, yeah. Meat. I love meat.

01:45.400 --> 01:47.960
Um, would you like to dance?

02:01.140 --> 02:04.220
I've always regretted what I said.

02:05.480 --> 02:11.230
When we first met, I said I 
wanted to give up on the test.

02:11.230 --> 02:18.240
I had no idea what you'd gone through 
or why you were climbing the Tower.

02:21.880 --> 02:24.740
The truth is, I met Dr. Sophia.

02:26.260 --> 02:29.750
She had continued her research.

02:29.940 --> 02:35.360
Does Dr. Sophia love me?

02:30.290 --> 02:32.680
On Living Ignition Weapons.

02:32.680 --> 02:35.400
Apparently they've made a finished product.

02:33.610 --> 02:41.260
<b>Emily
No.</b>

02:35.360 --> 02:41.260
<b>Emily
Dr. Sophia does not love you.</b>

02:35.860 --> 02:40.880
She knew what would happen 
to Cassano's and my bodies.

02:41.260 --> 02:45.740
If that love, that warm smile,

02:45.740 --> 02:50.580
and our names from my memories were 
all lies to advance her research,

02:50.580 --> 02:55.510
then do we really have no choice 
but to become real devils?

03:10.960 --> 03:16.900
<i>I see. I've already found 
the people who will save me.</i>

03:18.360 --> 03:19.410
Goseng.

03:21.100 --> 03:25.480
Once the tournament is over, 
may I rejoin all of you?

03:29.160 --> 03:30.980
Did anything happen?

03:32.140 --> 03:35.820
Nothing, huh? How very boring.

03:36.530 --> 03:37.980
Thank you.

03:38.880 --> 03:44.490
You took the others outside so my 
friends wouldn't be found, didn't you?

03:44.490 --> 03:47.410
Don't bother thanking me.

03:47.410 --> 03:50.600
I just wanted to know your 
relationship with them.

03:51.730 --> 03:53.580
I have something to tell you.

03:54.720 --> 03:58.600
I'll be leaving this team during 
the tournament tomorrow.

05:28.970 --> 05:32.970
<b>Episode 20</b>

05:28.970 --> 05:32.970
<b>Like a Flame in the Wind</b>

05:33.720 --> 05:36.980
Thank you for waiting, everyone.

05:36.980 --> 05:43.230
We will now hold a team tournament to 
determine the champions of the Workshop Battle!

05:44.390 --> 05:45.870
Here are the rules.

05:46.700 --> 05:50.180
Team Mad Dog vs. Team FUG 
will fight on the north side,

05:50.180 --> 05:52.930
while the other eight 
teams participate in the

05:52.930 --> 05:55.310
Development Tournament on the south side.

05:55.310 --> 06:01.010
The winners of both sides will 
then compete for the grand prize.

06:01.470 --> 06:05.990
In the Development Tournament,
each team's starter will gather points

06:05.990 --> 06:09.070
to summon allies and buy items.

06:09.070 --> 06:14.260
They advance to the next round by 
defeating their opponent's starter.

06:14.670 --> 06:18.390
Each team receives 50,000 
points every 30 minutes.

06:18.390 --> 06:21.880
Defeating an enemy awards 100,000 points.

06:21.880 --> 06:26.280
Defeating the starter awards 500,000 points.

06:26.750 --> 06:31.000
You're currently in the non-combat area.

06:31.000 --> 06:34.990
You'll have 30 minutes after the round begins

06:34.990 --> 06:37.290
to move to the combat 
area and begin fighting.

06:37.290 --> 06:40.290
Is everyone ready?

06:40.560 --> 06:43.540
The team tournament...

06:43.860 --> 06:45.840
...begins now!

06:48.190 --> 06:50.800
So, what do you think of this match?

06:50.800 --> 06:53.300
The problem is those two.

06:53.780 --> 06:55.940
It's not fair that there's two of them!

06:55.940 --> 06:59.060
In any case, we'll have to be careful 
about how we approach them.

06:59.290 --> 07:01.480
<i>We'll avoid crossing the bridge to attack.</i>

07:01.480 --> 07:04.060
You're screwed if you get sandwiched there.

07:04.380 --> 07:07.220
There's another route on the eastern shore.

07:07.220 --> 07:09.820
It'll take time, but circle around

07:10.170 --> 07:12.070
<i>and head directly to 
the summoning station.</i>

07:12.070 --> 07:13.820
What? We're summoning teammates?

07:14.080 --> 07:15.430
Who?

07:30.100 --> 07:32.090
<i>Nice work, Bundawan.</i>

07:32.090 --> 07:35.010
<i>Get some rest until we're 
down to the final four.</i>

07:40.100 --> 07:43.850
What was all that stuff yesterday about?

07:44.560 --> 07:46.680
There's something up with him.

07:46.680 --> 07:48.730
You mean Viole?

07:48.730 --> 07:51.310
I don't know exactly what it is, though.

07:51.310 --> 07:53.740
Huh? What does that mean?

07:54.060 --> 07:56.240
Well, you've been warned.

07:57.430 --> 07:59.750
Hey, wait! Anaak!

08:01.250 --> 08:04.750
<i>And when Endorsi came back late...</i>

08:06.160 --> 08:09.250
<i>I could feel the murderous energy coming 
off her when I tried to talk to her.</i>

08:13.600 --> 08:18.210
Now I know what it's like to be a father 
whose daughter gives him the cold shoulder.

08:18.210 --> 08:20.790
<i>We did it, leader!</i>

08:20.790 --> 08:21.960
Yeah!

08:22.760 --> 08:25.160
<i>All right, no more hesitating!</i>

08:25.160 --> 08:27.820
All right!

08:25.550 --> 08:29.270
<i>Let's get this match out the way 
so we can fight Viole's team!</i>

08:30.240 --> 08:31.870
If I may have your attention,

08:32.610 --> 08:37.280
I'll explain the rules of 
Team Mad Dog vs. Team FUG.

08:37.690 --> 08:40.240
Enshrined at the temple in 
the middle of this island

08:40.240 --> 08:44.680
is the key to the place where 
the grand prize is hidden.

08:44.680 --> 08:49.550
If Team FUG defeats Team Mad 
Dog and gets the key, they win!

08:49.550 --> 08:53.800
If Team Mad Dog successfully 
defends the key, they win!

08:56.970 --> 08:58.300
Reflejo,

08:59.140 --> 09:03.330
could you tell me again 
about this Baragav person?

09:03.770 --> 09:09.570
Baragav is one of three 
mad dogs Yama created.

09:09.980 --> 09:13.640
Mad dogs are produced through a 
technique called blood binding,

09:13.640 --> 09:18.820
which involves mixing and injecting 
at least two types of powerful blood.

09:19.320 --> 09:24.900
It allows mad dogs to acquire 
extraordinary power.

09:25.420 --> 09:27.490
He's incredibly dangerous.

09:27.940 --> 09:31.750
After defeating his teammates, 
together we should—

09:31.750 --> 09:33.840
I don't want to make any 
unnecessary sacrifices.

09:34.560 --> 09:37.590
Quickly capturing just the 
mad dog would be best.

09:38.800 --> 09:41.850
The rest of you, please stay back and defend.

09:42.400 --> 09:44.100
I will go face the mad dog...

09:44.840 --> 09:46.580
alone.

09:47.650 --> 09:49.600
Here we go!

09:49.950 --> 09:52.070
Let the match begin!

09:53.020 --> 09:55.380
We're finally here.

09:55.380 --> 09:58.610
<i>Don't let your guard down. 
The combat area is ahead.</i>

09:58.610 --> 10:01.360
<i>If you're unlucky, you'll be killed instantly.</i>

10:01.360 --> 10:05.370
Roger that. Let's hurry up 
and summon some teammates.

10:08.700 --> 10:10.630
<i>Welcome to the summoning station.</i>

10:12.630 --> 10:16.380
<i>I am R-7, your robot assistant.</i>

10:16.820 --> 10:19.640
<i>Allow me to explain how 
to summon your teammates.</i>

10:24.810 --> 10:26.890
<i>This is the summoning spring.</i>

10:27.320 --> 10:31.490
<i>Your teammates will appear in 
the spring at the cost of points.</i>

10:32.460 --> 10:34.150
Seriously?

10:34.150 --> 10:37.650
<i>You can even summon eliminated participants.</i>

10:38.300 --> 10:44.990
<i>Which means we can summon Bam 
if FUG loses to the mad dog.</i>

10:46.280 --> 10:48.160
So, who should we summon?

10:48.420 --> 10:50.550
<i>For now, we'll follow the plan.</i>

10:50.960 --> 10:52.420
Quaetro Blitz.

10:52.420 --> 10:55.800
What? That insane fire-user?

10:56.070 --> 10:58.800
He may be insane, but he's strong.

10:58.800 --> 11:01.300
Yeah, but his insanity is on another—

11:01.300 --> 11:03.570
<i>I thought I'd find you here.</i>

11:03.570 --> 11:04.810
It's them...

11:04.810 --> 11:07.430
<i>You bought a cheap starter</i>

11:07.430 --> 11:11.370
and came straight to the 
summoning station for allies.

11:11.370 --> 11:15.070
My sixth sense told me exactly 
what you had planned.

11:15.970 --> 11:18.320
<i>Wangnan, summon Quaetro!</i>

11:18.320 --> 11:19.070
Got it!

11:21.070 --> 11:23.320
Come to me, Quaetro Blitz!

11:24.440 --> 11:26.830
Huh? What is this?

11:27.170 --> 11:29.500
<i>Your teammate is now loading.</i>

11:29.500 --> 11:31.260
<i>What? Loading?</i>

11:31.260 --> 11:33.480
<i>Approximately five minutes to completion.</i>

11:33.480 --> 11:34.910
<i>You can't be serious!</i>

11:34.910 --> 11:36.670
Well, we're screwed...

11:47.790 --> 11:49.100
Something's not right.

11:49.490 --> 11:53.390
<i>They're holding back on purpose... 
to buy time? But why?</i>

11:59.080 --> 12:00.390
Steal the Thorn?

12:00.390 --> 12:05.870
Yeah. FUG entered three gamblers 
in this Workshop Battle.

12:06.370 --> 12:11.120
They intend to kill all your teammates 
while you're fighting the mad dog.

12:11.120 --> 12:15.130
There are FUG Rankers aboard the 
<i>Archimedes</i>. There's nowhere to run.

12:15.450 --> 12:19.800
In other words, stealing the Thorn 
is the only way to stop FUG.

12:22.380 --> 12:26.970
You can have it. It's a spare key 
that will take you to the Thorn.

12:26.970 --> 12:29.140
I stole it from the Workshop.

12:29.510 --> 12:32.120
<i>Come to the Thorn during the tournament.</i>

12:32.120 --> 12:34.700
<i>Then you'll understand everything.</i>

12:35.650 --> 12:38.960
<i>Both the truth hidden 
in this Workshop Battle</i>

12:38.960 --> 12:41.930
<i>and the way to be reunited 
with your friends.</i>

12:54.340 --> 12:58.430
Viole told us to stay back, Reflejo.

12:58.950 --> 13:01.920
You're working with the mad dog, aren't you?

13:08.190 --> 13:10.720
Anaak, are you feeling okay?

13:11.010 --> 13:12.820
I'm going to be fighting FUG tomorrow.

13:12.820 --> 13:14.850
I'll teach them a lesson on your behalf, too.

13:15.720 --> 13:18.610
Actually, there's something 
else you can do for me.

13:21.610 --> 13:24.240
Steal the Thorn? Easier said than done.

13:24.240 --> 13:25.480
Yoo-hoo!

13:26.110 --> 13:27.100
What do you want?

13:27.100 --> 13:29.140
You're not FUG, right?

13:29.570 --> 13:32.360
I have a message from Viole's friend.

13:32.940 --> 13:38.880
"If you'll leave your team, the mad 
dog might help you a teeny bit."

13:46.610 --> 13:50.850
It's a win-win. Team Mad Dog 
wants to bring down FUG,

13:51.450 --> 13:54.600
and Viole wants to leave FUG.

13:57.740 --> 14:02.210
You guys will fall here, and Viole 
will rejoin his old teammates...

14:02.520 --> 14:06.860
after stealing the Thorn 
you guys wanted so bad!

14:07.710 --> 14:09.740
Who do you think you are?

14:12.060 --> 14:15.750
You don't understand what I am.

14:16.370 --> 14:19.000
You little brat.

14:24.950 --> 14:26.630
What should we do, Khun?

14:26.630 --> 14:28.380
Run like your life depends on it.

14:28.610 --> 14:29.330
What?

14:31.940 --> 14:33.850
<i>In this cramped space?</i>

14:34.080 --> 14:36.430
Show them what you can do!

14:40.050 --> 14:43.150
One hit from that, and I'll 
be sent straight to hell!

14:44.330 --> 14:46.150
<i>There must be something.</i>

14:49.780 --> 14:51.200
<i>Two as one...</i>

14:51.700 --> 14:53.700
<i>Two as one...</i>

14:55.700 --> 14:59.240
<i>Two as one...</i>

15:00.440 --> 15:02.760
<i>Wangnan, run toward them.</i>

15:02.760 --> 15:03.770
Huh?

15:03.770 --> 15:05.210
<i>It's an experiment. Go!</i>

15:05.210 --> 15:07.240
<i>An experiment? Are you nuts?!</i>

15:07.240 --> 15:08.430
<i>If I do that—</i>

15:08.430 --> 15:11.220
It's the only way. Trust me.

15:12.310 --> 15:15.970
<i>Your only strength is 
your ridiculous courage!</i>

15:21.530 --> 15:24.700
Well, now I can't not do it.

15:24.700 --> 15:25.980
Damn it!

15:29.520 --> 15:30.610
Jump to the side!

15:36.790 --> 15:38.120
They stopped?

15:38.120 --> 15:40.620
I knew it. They're halves.

15:42.340 --> 15:45.380
It's been bothering me since 
the individual tournament.

15:45.740 --> 15:48.970
Yellow is always on the right, 
and blue is always on the left.

15:48.970 --> 15:50.340
I'd heard rumors about

15:50.340 --> 15:54.070
a people whose bodies are split in 
half living somewhere in the Tower.

15:54.070 --> 15:55.890
That must be them.

15:55.890 --> 15:58.260
So the remaining halves...

15:58.260 --> 15:59.450
...are decoys.

15:59.830 --> 16:04.770
That's why they couldn't respond right 
away when you entered their blind spot.

16:05.140 --> 16:08.530
Damn it... Kill him!

16:12.940 --> 16:14.030
Did we get him?

16:18.430 --> 16:20.790
Now that I know what you are...

16:26.200 --> 16:28.030
<i>The experiment was a success.</i>

16:28.030 --> 16:29.300
Who do you think you are?

16:29.300 --> 16:31.190
<i>Congratulations!</i>

16:31.190 --> 16:35.800
<i>You've defeated the opposing starter 
and advanced to the final four!</i>

16:37.330 --> 16:39.560
<i>Summoning Quaetro Blitz.</i>

16:43.580 --> 16:46.560
Quaetro Blitz, ruler of 
the flame, has arrived!

16:46.800 --> 16:48.200
You're late.

16:48.200 --> 16:50.970
Where's the human firewood you want burned?

16:50.970 --> 16:54.070
Khun, should we summon more people?

16:54.070 --> 16:56.070
Let me think...

17:02.660 --> 17:04.830
Dinosaur!

17:04.830 --> 17:07.330
Should've summoned me sooner.

17:07.970 --> 17:11.910
<i>So people can be summoned instantly 
once the match is over.</i>

17:11.910 --> 17:14.590
So, how's the Black Turtle?

17:14.590 --> 17:15.820
I don't know.

17:16.260 --> 17:19.040
We can only view the results from here.

17:19.040 --> 17:21.350
Maybe from the waiting room TV...

17:21.350 --> 17:23.330
<i>The waiting room!</i>

17:23.330 --> 17:25.310
Stay safe, Bam.

17:25.310 --> 17:27.830
Stay safe, Black Turtle.

17:33.620 --> 17:34.430
So this...

17:34.430 --> 17:39.620
Apparently FUG calls it 
the kingslaying Thorn.

17:39.620 --> 17:46.870
Long ago, Enryu the Irregular came to the 
Tower and killed a floor administrator.

17:46.870 --> 17:51.590
The shocking incident shattered 
the ironclad notion

17:51.590 --> 17:53.630
that administrators were invincible.

17:54.300 --> 17:58.640
This Thorn was found at the location 
where Enryu killed the administrator.

17:58.920 --> 18:05.930
FUG thought they could use this 
to kill Jahad, but they couldn't...

18:05.930 --> 18:08.240
because it was already dead.

18:09.550 --> 18:12.770
In order to use this Ignition Weapon 
that's no more than a shell now,

18:12.770 --> 18:15.710
FUG worked with Workshop scientists.

18:15.710 --> 18:20.550
They promised to hand over ownership of 
the Thorn and fully back their research.

18:21.290 --> 18:25.830
The Workshop indiscriminately kidnapped 
illegitimate children from the Middle Area

18:25.830 --> 18:27.650
and began their research...

18:29.080 --> 18:32.100
on turning humans into Ignition Weapons.

18:32.890 --> 18:35.300
The kingslaying Thorn?

18:35.690 --> 18:39.230
It's the key to fulfilling 
FUG's greatest wish.

18:39.230 --> 18:43.390
We've spent years trying 
to achieve that goal.

18:43.390 --> 18:46.310
And finally, we found the last ingredient.

18:46.310 --> 18:51.920
We've been preparing for this 
for far longer than you realize.

18:52.230 --> 18:56.570
All that's left is to hand over the 
completed weapon to my master.

18:56.570 --> 18:59.650
Oh, come on. What nonsense is—

19:00.380 --> 19:06.450
We're still in total control 
of this Workshop Tournament.

19:06.450 --> 19:10.710
You're the ones caught in our trap, brat.

19:10.980 --> 19:14.160
Our research was conducted in secret.

19:14.160 --> 19:18.970
Experimenting on living humans is 
forbidden within the Workshop, as well.

19:18.970 --> 19:20.970
But that didn't stop them.

19:21.630 --> 19:24.720
Obsessed with their research, 
they finally succeeded

19:24.720 --> 19:29.730
at recreating humans as 
Living Ignition Weapons.

19:30.740 --> 19:34.980
Why were they so obsessed 
with Living Ignition Weapons?

19:35.290 --> 19:41.240
Because they'd acquired a devil 
that could activate the Thorn.

19:41.240 --> 19:44.310
The one inside you.

19:45.240 --> 19:50.750
I don't know the specifics, but they say 
the devil inside you once rivaled the gods.

19:50.750 --> 19:56.750
The purpose of their research was to grant 
you the power to activate this Thorn.

19:56.750 --> 19:59.270
That's how you were made.

20:00.260 --> 20:04.730
FUG planned to give you the 
Thorn at this Workshop Battle,

20:04.730 --> 20:07.450
but a group of Slayers opposed the idea.

20:07.450 --> 20:10.020
They said you might betray them.

20:10.020 --> 20:13.580
So they came up with the idea 
to create an Ignition Weapon by

20:13.580 --> 20:16.520
imbuing a Thorn's shell with a soul

20:16.520 --> 20:19.620
and return it to themselves.

20:19.960 --> 20:25.030
The grand prize of this Workshop Battle,
Jue Viole Grace!

20:33.310 --> 20:35.670
You're the mad dog's...

20:35.670 --> 20:37.870
You really are pure, aren't you?

20:39.420 --> 20:43.680
You and Anaak were FUG's 
pawns from the start.

20:44.220 --> 20:45.680
What's going on here?

20:45.680 --> 20:47.630
You said you hated FUG!

20:47.630 --> 20:51.430
It was all an act to trap Jue Viole Grace.

20:51.430 --> 20:53.000
Didn't I tell you?

20:53.000 --> 20:55.410
He'd only help you a teeny bit.

20:55.990 --> 20:57.440
Kill him.

21:07.620 --> 21:09.620
What's going on here?

21:10.620 --> 21:12.420
Run! It's a trap!

21:13.410 --> 21:14.910
Get down!

21:24.170 --> 21:25.680
Should we go after them?

21:25.680 --> 21:31.000
Ignore them. There's nothing they can do.

21:31.430 --> 21:32.880
What's going on?

21:32.880 --> 21:37.360
It's a setup. FUG and the mad dog 
were working together from the start.

21:37.360 --> 21:38.190
What?

21:38.190 --> 21:41.670
They're trying to use Viole to do something.

21:47.410 --> 21:48.750
Are you here to get in my way?

21:48.750 --> 21:49.950
Follow me.

21:50.390 --> 21:52.860
I'd like you two to do something for me.

23:38.250 --> 23:40.940
He can do that, too?

23:38.990 --> 23:41.250
<b>Next Time
The Beginning of Dawn</b>
